usage_tracking.description:
Home Assistant can count your kilowatt hours into a separate total for each rate, so you can see how much you used at each price. That is a Utility Meter helper: it makes one total per rate, plus a dropdown saying which total is currently counting.

Nothing moves that dropdown on its own, so people normally write an automation for it. This screen can create the helper and keep the dropdown pointed at the rate in force, which is the only thing this integration ever writes.

